of her necklaces  and the many large and small ones on  this dress here  it's certainly fitting that the show  associates butterflies with the  featheringtons as not only are the  insects often highly colourful but also  because of their short lifespans and  ephemeral beauty  they can be symbols of empty vanity as  to why they're linked to penelope in  particular  the fact butterflies often symbolize  transformation  freedom and new beginnings is a hint  that penelope's not exactly what at  first she appears to be  at the beginning of the show she seems  to be a debutant that few people pay  attention to penelope i did not see you  there but by the end of season one  our perception of her has been  transformed as we discover that she's  the author of society's most popular  scandal sheet  whose words everyone listens to and  thanks to that secret identity she  enjoys a level of freedom she never had  before  a scribbling woman is the most canine if  that should be true  then this author would like to show you  her teeth when it came to dressing the  featherington family costume designer  ella mirage nick went deliberately over  the top  aiming for a gaudy over decorated  overzealous look to convey the fact  their nouveau riche  and to create a sharp contrast with the  refinement of the more well-established  bridgeton family  so feathering to matriarch porsche goes  for bright colours  bold patterns and lots of embellishments  and she wants her daughters to stand out  so she can marry them off  the bridgeton family's look is more  elegant and muted  leaning into a pretty pristine powdery  palette of pale blues  silvers and greens and when it comes to  daphne specifically as her character  matures she goes for duskier colours  with  richer pinks and blues and deeper  silvers as costume designer miroznik  puts it she begins as a porcelain doll  and becomes a woman  as for eloise who's smart rebellious and  speaks her mind perhaps you should like  me to picture  her clothes tend to be simple in shape  and quite covered up  and rather than being sent out and  decorated she gets what the designer  calls a masculine twist  then the simon whose rich velvet fabrics  and brocades as well as the colours  patterns and cuts of his clothes stand  out as they're influenced by his travels  abroad according to mirage nick  reds and golds which are his family  colours in the novels are quite often  part of his outfits though according to  the costume designer the real reason for  that  is that the very first time they tried  red on actor reggae jean-page in a  fitting he just looks so good in it  on top of that leficialusa.com describes  simon's darker mature palette as  providing a contrast to daphne's frothy  pieces which points towards the dynamic  of their relationship  and if you're wondering about the  significance of the diamond and emerald  encrusted in our brooch that simon can  often be seen wearing on his lapel  it belonged to his late mother so acts  as a reminder of her  due to sharoner chris van dusen's  obsession with the bbc adaptation of  pride and prejudice from the 1990s  simon gets his very own mr darcy style  moment  though van dusen wanted to see a period  piece that went even further than that  so this time the wet white shirt isn't  caused by plunging into a lake  instead simon gets caught in a sudden  downpour during some alfresco  late night loving with his new wife  tulips are mentioned a few times in the  show but this exchange between violet  bridgeton and her son anthony  particularly caught my attention  tulips they symbolize passion most  appropriate hem for your sister when she  decides to marry the duke  perhaps your bride would like the same  this seemingly small moment is very  significant as it's a big clue to what  will happen in season two of the show  why is that well because it's a hat tip  to the novels where violet has filled  the garden of her country home with one  of her favorite flowers tulips  and in the second book of the bridgeton  saga anthony picks a tulip for his new  love interest  so in the first episode during one of  anthony's trysts with sienna when you  see his watch on this piece of furniture  with a tulip-like design  it's a subtle hint that his time with  her will soon be over  as his new love interest in the second  season will be the woman he gives a  tulip to  in the books when anthony tells his  youngest sister hyacinths she can join  in with the summer fun at their country  home  as long as she stays clear of his lucky  mallet that's a nod to the croquet-like  game of pal mal that the bridgeton's  love to play in the novels and has  become a real fan favorite moment  according to author julia quinn  that game which in the second novel  daphne says is full of bad sportsmanship  cheating and lying and is less about  winning than making sure the other  players lose plays an important role in  anthony's love life so it'll very likely  pop up in the second season  especially as quinn our showrunner  vandusen to make sure it does  during a flashback to simon's childhood  we learn his father had him hidden away  because of his stammer  instead of going to school then his  governors taught him and his lessons  included latin which was usual for boys  at the time  an interesting detail that signals the  kind of man simon will grow up to be are  the latin conjugations on the blackboard  for the word pugnare which means to  fight to battle to strive or struggle  as a child simon strove to overcome his  stammer and lack of confidence with the  help of lady danbury  and as an adult he not only gets  involved in boxing but he also ends up  in a jewel with anthony  so this shot shows how simon has in a  way been learning the meaning of  fighting since he was a child  during a raunchy rendezvous it's no  coincidence that anthony crashes into a  poster for mozart's opera don giovanni  on sienna's dressing room wall that  particular opera is based on the legend  of don juan a young licentious nobleman  who places pleasure above all  else which anthony certainly does for  much of the first season  you like to speak of responsibility my  dear son  pray tell what should you know of it the  way the framed poster tumbles to the  floor could also be a little hint to how  anthony and siena's relationship  will eventually come crashing down the  line for three nights only on the poster  also foreshadows the temporary nature of  their affair  there's another clever bit of  foreshadowing on the dance cards and the  ballroom floor at danbury house where a  latin phrase appears which means we do  not learn for school but for life  this fits the show well because as  showrunner van dusen says season one  focuses on the education of daphne  bridgeton  who starts out as this young innocent  debutant who knows very little of love  and nothing of sex  titled chaste and innocent this is what  they have been raised and trained for  since  birth then as van dusen says over the  course of the series we watch her  transform entirely  now what did you think of bridgeton and  did you notice any little details or  easter eggs leave your comments below  and if you enjoyed this don't forget to  leave a thumbs up it's hugely  appreciated  tap left for my next netflix video  including a full breakdown of the  sabrina series finale and a potential  part 5  or tap right for something else you're  sure to like thanks for watching and see  you next time yippee kai movie lovers
 

